{
  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed Airbnb has the potential to increase activity level and coming and goings to and from the site, due &lt;span style=&quot;font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt;&quot;&gt;a&amp;nbsp;frequent turnover of occupants, consequently&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;resulting in additional levels of noise and disturbance at the property. The proposal is therefore likely to have a negative impact on neighbouring amenity in this street of family housing and in turn the health and wellbeing of neighbouring residents. This is especially the case considering the applicant failed to&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt;&quot;&gt;demonstrate that the Airbnb would&amp;nbsp;not have significant adverse impact on surrounding amenity.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;As such the proposal is contrary to the following:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif&quot;&gt;Policies D6, D14 and&amp;nbsp;GG3 of the London Plan (2021)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;Policies DMD1,&amp;nbsp;DMH5, DME4 and DMSI3 of the Local Plan (September 2024)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;",
    "&lt;p style=&quot;&quot;&gt;The proposed development results in the loss of a family-sized dwellinghouse, the need for which is clearly demonstrated in the development plan and supporting evidence base.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;For this reason, the negatives arising from the proposal, in association with the&amp;nbsp;detrimental impact on the borough&#x27;s supply of family housing,&amp;nbsp;are considered to outweigh any significant benefits. The principle of development is therefore considered unacceptable and contrary to&amp;nbsp;the following policies:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;National Planning Policy Framework (December 2024)&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;Policy&amp;nbsp;DMH4 and strategic policies&amp;nbsp;SP3 and&amp;nbsp;SPDG1 of the Barking and Dagenham Local Plan 2037 (September 2024)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed development, by reason of its location does not sit within a focused town centres or opportunity area. Therefore the proposed development is considered a non conforming use within this location which is contrary to the following policies:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;Policy E10 of the&amp;nbsp;London Plan (March 2021); &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;Policies DME3 and DME4 of The London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Local Plan 2037 (September 2024)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;"
  ],
